{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>When they offered strange fire.</b> For this alone was found in them." "<b>And they had no sons.</b> For if they had had sons to fill their place, they would have inherited the rank fitting their father." "<b>And Elazar and Itamar ministered.</b> He gave them appointment and authority in the Mishkan by the command of the blessed El." "<b>Before Aaron their father.</b> During Aaron's lifetime there was the anointing of the sons and the death of some of them and the authority of some of them — not by his word, even though he was High Priest. And all this does not persist for generations, for there is no anointing for an ordinary priest, nor does he receive appointment except through the High Priest during his lifetime."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:38.190083815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}